From 2a8dd5b8e2a3993f74e1b86e7a7768e735c7e674 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:02:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: drain startup work before parent
 detach

PDR and SSR notifications queue ngd_up_work on the system workqueue.
Releasing those providers stops new notifications, but already queued or
running startup work can still use the NGD child while the parent remove
path unregisters that child and releases its state.

Cancel and join startup work after both notification providers have
stopped and before unregistering the NGD child. Six synthetic parent
removal cases execute the exact callbacks with queued work, a blocked
running worker and callbacks finishing during provider release. Ten
ordering checks fail before the change and none fail afterward. Devices,
providers, QMI, DMA and the workqueue are models backed by pthreads.
Child-only unbind, master work, IRQ/DMA quiescence and physical acceptance
remain separate work.

OpenAI Codex implemented the fix, changelog and host qualification.
Human review and DCO certification are pending.

Fixes: a899d324863a ("slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: add Sub System Restart support")
---
 drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
index a4eba5aa9..8fadc5847 100644
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -1778,6 +1778,7 @@ static void qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	pdr_handle_release(ctrl->pdr);
 	qcom_unregister_ssr_notifier(ctrl->notifier, &ctrl->nb);
+	cancel_work_sync(&ctrl->ngd_up_work);
 
 	qcom_slim_ngd_unregister(ctrl);
 
